Licensing
=========

Copyright © Akhil Wali

This repository holds both a static site generator and the writing it publishes.
Each scope below is licensed as a whole. Where more than one of the statements
below could apply to a file, the more specific one governs.

The generator is under the Eclipse Public License, Version 1.0, the full text of
which is in LICENSES/EPL-1.0.txt. This covers src/, themes/, config/, README.md,
deps.edn, flake.nix, flake.lock, .envrc, REUSE.toml, .gitignore and .gitmodules.
themes/ is derived from the "blue" theme distributed with Cryogen
(https://github.com/cryogen-project/cryogen), copyright © the Cryogen
contributors. The templates there have been modified (restructured for Bootstrap
4, with markup, metadata and asset handling changed throughout) and those
modifications are contributed under the same license.

web/ is under the MIT License, the full text of which is in LICENSES/MIT.txt.
This covers the scripts, stylesheets and build configuration of the npm project
there. web/vendor/ is third-party code and is not mine to relicense; each file
there is accompanied by a .license file of the same name, carrying that file's
own copyright notice and license terms.

Posts, pages and images are under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International License, the full text of which is in
LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt. This covers everything under content/.

Code snippets are under the MIT No Attribution License (MIT-0), the full text of
which is in LICENSES/MIT-0.txt. This covers every fenced code block in the posts
and pages under content/md/. Blocks carry no individual license marking; the
grant is blanket. Where a block was quoted from somewhere else, it is identified
as such in the surrounding prose, and it is governed by its own terms rather
than by this grant.

These scopes are also expressed as SPDX tags in REUSE.toml, so the repository is
readable by REUSE tooling. That file is kept in sync with this one, not the
other way round: wherever the two disagree, this statement governs. SPDX cannot
describe a license split inside a single file, so REUSE.toml names both
CC-BY-SA-4.0 and MIT-0 for content/ and leaves the line between them to the
paragraph above.

LICENSE is this statement, LICENSES/ holds the verbatim texts it refers to, and
the .license files in web/vendor/ hold the terms of the code beside them. None
of these are covered by the grants above; each text is reproduced under whatever
terms its own steward sets for verbatim copying.

public/ is generated output, produced from content/, themes/ and web/. As the
holder of copyright in the content, I offer the post and page text and the
images as they appear there under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International License. The surrounding template markup remains under
EPL-1.0, and the compiled scripts and stylesheets remain under the MIT License.
Assets copied or bundled into public/ keep their own licenses:

  - public/fonts/*.woff2 are under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1.
    Alegreya Sans is copyright © 2013 The Alegreya Sans Project Authors;
    Cascadia Code is copyright © 2019 - Present, Microsoft Corporation, with
    Reserved Font Name Cascadia Code.
    Both notices and the license text are emitted together into
    public/fonts/LICENSE.txt, so that they travel with the fonts.

  - public/css/darth10.github.io.css includes the "base16/solarized-dark" theme
    distributed with highlight.js, by Ethan Schoonover and modified by
    aramisgithub, taken from base16-schemes-source and offered there under MIT
    or more permissive terms. The theme's CSS is included unminified, so its own
    notice survives as a comment inside the stylesheet.

  - public/js/darth10.github.io.min.js bundles highlight.js, copyright © 2006
    Ivan Sagalaev, released under the BSD 3-Clause License; and Turbo
    (https://turbo.hotwired.dev), copyright © 37signals LLC, released under the
    MIT License.

  - public/posts/*/post.min.js bundle Flot, copyright © 2007-2014 IOLA and Ole
    Laursen, under the MIT License, together with the color helpers inlined into
    each bundle, released under the MIT License by Ole Laursen, October 2009.
    Some posts additionally include plugins from web/vendor/, which carry their
    own terms alongside them as described above.

The copyright notice that each bundle above ships with is extracted verbatim
into the .LICENSE.txt file emitted beside it. Those notices do not themselves
carry the permission text that the MIT License requires to accompany copies, so
public/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt collects each notice together with the full text
of the license it names, or a pointer to where that text is served. LICENSES/
holds only the licenses this repository's own files are under; the texts for the
bundled code above are taken from the packages that ship them at build time.
